1
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:08,700
- Are you here for the job offer ceremony, too?
- Yeah.

2
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:10,880
Have you decided which
department you want to join?

3
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:13,750
- I'm hoping for PR.
- I see.

4
00:00:22,810 --> 00:00:24,690
Excuse me, hold the elevator!

5
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:33,400
Excuse me.

6
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,540
Looking forward to working with you.

7
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:43,370
Likewise.

8
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:10,099
(6 Years Later)

9
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,400
(Chikubeni Co., Ltd.)

10
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:16,000
Is your calculator broken, Kanda-san?

11
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:21,340
The settlement for this
travel advance is off.

12
00:01:21,690 --> 00:01:23,750
That's the third time this month.

13
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:25,850
Huh?

14
00:01:29,770 --> 00:01:30,770
That's weird.

15
00:01:31,690 --> 00:01:32,690
Oh, you're right.

16
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:35,090
Don't "oh, you're right" me.

17
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:36,800
Please fix it immediately.

18
00:01:36,850 --> 00:01:38,290
Have it done before you leave today.

19
00:01:38,850 --> 00:01:39,850
That is all.

20
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,970
Ah, wait, hold on!

21
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:47,860
Don't be so mad.

22
00:01:48,110 --> 00:01:49,310
So impatient.

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,890
I'll fix it right now, just give me a sec.

24
00:01:53,510 --> 00:01:58,040
Let's see, travel
advance, travel advance...

25
00:01:58,550 --> 00:01:59,550
First, right here.

26
00:02:09,010 --> 00:02:10,450
Just watching them makes me nervous.

27
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:13,630
Ueno-san is really strict, isn't he?

28
00:02:14,490 --> 00:02:17,280
Everyone in Accounting is
by-the-book, especially him.

29
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:19,010
Ueno-san isn't the issue here.

30
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:21,870
Don't you think Kanda-san
is acting a bit strange?

31
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:24,369
How so?

32
00:02:24,370 --> 00:02:25,930
We're talking about the Kanda-san here.

33
00:02:28,610 --> 00:02:31,310
He won the company sales
competition in his second year.

34
00:02:34,670 --> 00:02:36,370
His numbers are always at the top.

35
00:02:37,290 --> 00:02:40,170
He's only in his twenties, and he's
already a top contender for manager.

36
00:02:40,590 --> 00:02:41,590
I'll keep doing my best.

37
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:43,300
Thank you, everyone.

38
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:48,370
He normally never messes up his paperwork.

39
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:51,666
Despite how he looks,
he's actually super thorough.

40
00:02:51,690 --> 00:02:55,260
He is the ace of the
Sales Department, after all.

41
00:02:55,570 --> 00:02:57,050
And yet...

42
00:02:57,950 --> 00:03:00,350
Whenever it comes to accounting,
Ueno's always chewing him out.

43
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:04,370
- And always over rookie mistakes, too.
- What are you getting at?

44
00:03:04,510 --> 00:03:08,480
Well, maybe Kanda-san
actually hates Ueno-san's guts,

45
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,920
and he's messing up on purpose
just to give him a hard time.

46
00:03:11,570 --> 00:03:13,490
Kanda-san would never
do something like that.

47
00:03:14,990 --> 00:03:18,190
I won't let you slander my bias like that.

48
00:03:18,650 --> 00:03:20,870
Your bias? Hey, you never know.

49
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:23,170
You're so annoying, you always... Oh.

50
00:03:25,770 --> 00:03:28,080
Shima-san, you can't expense this.

51
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:30,010
And the purpose isn't
stated clearly enough.

52
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:31,590
Go read the company guidelines...

53
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:35,470
Please.

54
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:37,890
Right, I'm sorry.

55
00:03:40,910 --> 00:03:42,750
That's what you get for running your mouth.

56
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:46,770
It's been three years since
I transferred to Accounting.

57
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,790
Before that, I used to be in Sales, too.

58
00:03:52,150 --> 00:03:55,230
Though at this point, practically
no one remembers that.

59
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:57,370
I'm an accountant through and through now.

60
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:20,820
I'm ho...

61
00:04:26,450 --> 00:04:28,290
Not again...

62
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,870
Hey, what do you think you're...

63
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,880
Oh, welcome back.

64
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:44,270
"You Should Be The One To Come Kiss Me"

65
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:47,799
(Episode 1)

66
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,800
Huh?

67
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:57,140
What are you doing
walking around like that?!

68
00:06:00,050 --> 00:06:01,050
Sorry, my bad.

69
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:03,650
I didn't expect you back so soon.

70
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:07,940
For starters, don't walk around
butt naked in someone else's house!

71
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:10,220
Being naked in someone
else's place is the best part.

72
00:06:13,110 --> 00:06:14,110
Kanda.

73
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:18,280
Seriously, knock it off.

74
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:25,060
Fine, I get it.

75
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:27,050
I'm sorry, okay?

76
00:06:32,890 --> 00:06:33,890
Ooh!

77
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:35,680
You've got beer.

78
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:39,849
Put your underwear on first!

79
00:06:39,850 --> 00:06:40,900
Okay!

80
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:51,230
For the record, I'm gay.

81
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,220
And as for...

82
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:58,370
this straight guy who makes
himself right at home in my apartment,

83
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,970
he knows it, too.

84
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:12,140
Ahh!

85
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:15,780
Beer always tastes better
when you buy it, Ueno.

86
00:07:20,550 --> 00:07:21,620
So good.

87
00:07:24,710 --> 00:07:26,110
Is that supposed to be a dig at me?

88
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:29,030
It all started

89
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:31,320
back when I was still
in the Sales Department.

90
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:56,850
Kanda.

91
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:00,030
Still working late?

92
00:08:00,850 --> 00:08:01,850
Yeah.

93
00:08:04,030 --> 00:08:05,030
What about you?

94
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:06,760
Forget something?

95
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,600
No.

96
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:11,840
I figured I'd just crash at the office.

97
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,060
Huh?

98
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:17,970
There's a power outage or short
circuit at my building, or something.

99
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:21,640
They're still inspecting
it, so I can't go home.

100
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:27,290
I was gonna crash at a friend's
place, but his girlfriend's coming over.

101
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:34,330
What about a hotel?

102
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:36,990
That's a waste of money.

103
00:08:44,694 --> 00:08:45,950
Sorry, I got it dirty.

104
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:49,120
It's fine.

105
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:58,080
I should've bought a towel on the way here.

106
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:07,140
Want to stay at my place?

107
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:08,880
It's close by, anyway.

108
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,860
After that, for some reason,
he just latched onto me.

109
00:10:22,030 --> 00:10:25,260
Before I knew it, he was sleeping
over at my place almost every week.

110
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:01,660
Hey.

111
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:04,850
Stop staring at me. You're way too close.

112
00:11:05,330 --> 00:11:06,330
Hmm?

113
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,060
Oh, sorry.

114
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:16,610
No, it's just...

115
00:11:18,170 --> 00:11:20,010
I think I see a gray hair.

116
00:11:21,470 --> 00:11:22,470
What?!

117
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:25,060
Where?

118
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:28,130
- Where is it?
- Let me see.

119
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,400
Huh?

120
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:36,650
Whoa...

121
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:38,810
There's a bunch of them.

122
00:11:40,010 --> 00:11:41,010
What?!

123
00:11:41,530 --> 00:11:42,650
You've got to be kidding me.

124
00:11:47,050 --> 00:11:48,830
Gotcha!

125
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,970
Man, Ueno, you're way too gullible.

126
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:53,300
I'm hitting the bathroom.

127
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,010
Someone's at the door.

128
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:09,560
Coming.

129
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:11,480
Delivery from Yamaneko Express.

130
00:12:12,730 --> 00:12:13,730
Alright.

131
00:12:24,570 --> 00:12:27,200
Another package came for you.

132
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:31,530
Oh right, I totally forgot. Thanks!

133
00:12:31,740 --> 00:12:32,980
Don't "thanks" me.

134
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:35,000
Huh?

135
00:12:46,050 --> 00:12:49,030
I ordered this during a sale the other day.

136
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:51,640
Why did you have it shipped to my place?

137
00:12:51,850 --> 00:12:54,330
I was gonna bring it over here anyway.

138
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:55,640
Wanna play a game?

139
00:12:59,410 --> 00:13:00,420
Of course.

140
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:03,710
If it weren't for you, I
never would've bought it.

141
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,200
I'd have no use for it.

142
00:13:07,070 --> 00:13:11,510
Kanda was like this even before I
came out to him. He hasn't changed a bit.

143
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:21,890
Hey, quit taking over my
shelves without asking.

144
00:13:21,970 --> 00:13:23,576
What's the big deal? The
space was empty anyway.

145
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:25,170
It's called interior design, okay?

146
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,870
Don't be so stingy.

147
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:27,920
Just hold on a sec.

148
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:29,716
I'll line up all the corners
nice and neat for you.

149
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:31,290
Lining up the corners isn't the point!

150
00:13:31,350 --> 00:13:32,818
Come on, I know how
picky you are about details.

151
00:13:32,842 --> 00:13:34,346
If anything, he's
only gotten pushier.

152
00:13:34,370 --> 00:13:35,730
What kind of idiot puts stuff
right in front of the speaker?

153
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:37,460
Who cares? They're both rectangular anyway.

154
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:38,900
Just put it over here for now.

155
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:42,000
You can't even see it
there. That's no fun...

156
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:50,030
You're off by a digit on
the billing amount here, too.

157
00:13:50,950 --> 00:13:51,730
Sorry.

158
00:13:51,810 --> 00:13:52,910
Please fix it.

159
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:54,616
Yes, sir! I'll have it fixed
by the end of the week.

160
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:55,640
By the end of the day.

161
00:13:57,790 --> 00:13:59,460
- Ah, Shirai-san.
- Yes?

162
00:13:59,710 --> 00:14:01,710
- Here.
- Oh, thank you.

163
00:14:03,710 --> 00:14:09,050
I'll stop by to visit you again next week.

164
00:14:09,330 --> 00:14:10,330
Sounds good.

165
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:11,800
Thank you for your time.

166
00:14:13,110 --> 00:14:14,110
Kanda.

167
00:14:14,850 --> 00:14:15,850
Yes?

168
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:26,130
Back again, Ueno? Accounting sure is tough.

169
00:14:26,470 --> 00:14:29,230
Mizoguchi, and Kobayashi. Long time no see.

170
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:30,470
Long time no see.

171
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:32,490
Rare to see you two paired up.

172
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:36,490
The company newsletter is doing a
feature on the new recruits in Sales.

173
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:38,416
The section chief threw me under the bus.

174
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,640
Let's make the headline,

175
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,750
"The Next Ace of the Sales Department."

176
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:44,190
"Leave the Numbers to Me!" How's that?

177
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:45,380
Very funny.

178
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:48,690
It's an honor to be in the newsletter.

179
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,400
- Way to go!
- Thank you!

180
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:55,180
- Is it true?
- Yeah!

181
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:56,180
Whoa!

182
00:15:02,150 --> 00:15:05,430
Maybe a peace sign is a
bit much. Thanks, everyone.

183
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,410
Speak of the reigning ace of Sales.

184
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,950
Kanda-senpai just landed
the Lanau Corp contract!

185
00:15:11,690 --> 00:15:13,256
He actually closed the
deal with Lanau Corp...?

186
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,280
Yeah.

187
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:17,540
That single deal just hit our
department's target for the whole quarter.

188
00:15:17,870 --> 00:15:18,910
That's insane.

189
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:20,950
Let's get him to treat us next time.

190
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:22,850
Shouldn't we be treating him?

191
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,670
Details, details.

192
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,240
Yo!

193
00:16:03,250 --> 00:16:05,120
This one's going up.

194
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:06,710
You could've told me sooner.

195
00:16:13,050 --> 00:16:15,390
Heard you landed the Lanau contract.

196
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:18,140
Oh, word got around?

197
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:22,190
I'm seriously carrying this
company on my back, huh?

198
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:26,810
So come on, Ueno, shower me with praise.

199
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,280
Congrats.

200
00:16:36,030 --> 00:16:37,030
What the heck?

201
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,720
You call that congratulating me?

202
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:42,160
Con-grats.

203
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:43,370
Just two syllables?

204
00:16:48,130 --> 00:16:53,140
Come on, even someone on the street would
at least give me the full "congratulations"!

205
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,890
Can't you put a little more effort into it?

206
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:58,560
Fine, fine.

207
00:16:59,770 --> 00:17:01,220
Con-grat-u-la-tions.

208
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:03,890
Zero emotion.

209
00:17:07,490 --> 00:17:08,580
Sorry, sorry.

210
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:13,170
I really am happy for you, though.

211
00:17:21,010 --> 00:17:22,010
In that case,

212
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:24,930
I'll send you my wish
list in the next few days.

213
00:17:27,690 --> 00:17:28,690
Huh?

214
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:30,080
Wish list?

215
00:17:32,490 --> 00:17:33,690
This is your floor, Ueno.

216
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:36,140
Oh.

217
00:18:12,490 --> 00:18:13,890
Keep up the good work.

218
00:18:14,270 --> 00:18:16,650
[Kanda:] Here's that wish list I mentioned.

219
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,580
It's nothing but cheap snacks.

220
00:18:32,610 --> 00:18:34,330
What goes on in that guy's head...

221
00:19:13,870 --> 00:19:14,870
Welcome.

222
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:33,590
Would it be weird...

223
00:19:34,610 --> 00:19:37,960
to buy a tie for a friend?

224
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:42,780
I'm really clueless
about this kind of thing...

225
00:19:44,940 --> 00:19:45,940
Still,

226
00:19:46,570 --> 00:19:48,320
seeing how hard he works every day,

227
00:19:49,470 --> 00:19:51,830
makes me want to get him
something special once in a while.

228
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:56,300
I just want...

229
00:19:58,430 --> 00:20:00,380
to see an even bigger smile on his face.

230
00:20:10,670 --> 00:20:11,670
Excuse me.

231
00:20:44,830 --> 00:20:46,070
That was close.

232
00:20:48,290 --> 00:20:51,570
I almost got carried away again.

233
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:06,390
I should just stick to the cheap snacks.

234
00:21:07,450 --> 00:21:09,260
He was just joking around anyway.

235
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:14,560
If I do anything to ruin what we have now,

236
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:17,240
I'm sure...

237
00:21:18,670 --> 00:21:20,310
he'll stop coming over altogether.

238
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:46,800
I'm beat.

239
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:50,200
Who calls at an hour like this?

240
00:21:53,230 --> 00:21:55,110
- Good work today.
- You too.

241
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,400
Got it.

242
00:22:01,730 --> 00:22:03,430
- Is something wrong?
- Huh?

243
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:06,560
Oh.

244
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,240
It's nothing.

245
00:22:10,210 --> 00:22:11,410
"Nothing," huh...

246
00:22:29,380 --> 00:22:30,830
Don't say anything I shouldn't.

247
00:22:31,890 --> 00:22:33,090
Don't do anything I shouldn't.

248
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:40,640
I've been letting him get too close lately.

249
00:22:42,010 --> 00:22:43,110
I need to be more careful.

250
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:51,340
Ah!

251
00:22:56,420 --> 00:22:57,620
Shoot.

252
00:22:58,890 --> 00:23:00,200
Missed it.

253
00:23:20,130 --> 00:23:21,130
Hey.

254
00:23:21,630 --> 00:23:22,930
Can I come over tonight?

255
00:23:29,070 --> 00:23:30,270
Here we go again...

256
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:47,040
(Next Episode Preview)
Are you and Ueno-san close, Kanda-senpai?

257
00:23:47,260 --> 00:23:49,560
Didn't I tell you not
to talk to me at work?

258
00:23:49,860 --> 00:23:51,400
Actually, I'm gay, too.

259
00:23:52,860 --> 00:23:54,420
Then can I come over to your place?

260
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:56,720
Last time was just a coincidence.

261
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:58,800
Kanda-san and I aren't actually that close.
